### Register a new player
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

### Register the same name again → 409 USERNAME_TAKEN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

### Bad input → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "c!", "password": "short"}

### Login OK → token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

### Wrong password → 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "wrongpass1"}

### Unknown user → also 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS (same message!)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "nobody", "password": "password123"}

### Login and save the token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "charlie", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### My wallet: WITH token → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My wallet: NO token → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me

### My wallet: FAKE token → 401 TOKEN_INVALID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxIn0.fakesignature

### My profile → 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Old URL is gone, even WITH a token → 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}